From 2f660611f86b913ce0158f87592c8a3e0ad2f0b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: codEx Fork Bot <codex-fork-bot@localhost>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:44:47 +0800
Subject: rewind: harden snapshot capture and restore edge cases

Harden the rewind snapshot engine against the edge cases found during
review:

- Never follow symbolic links during restore: a link at the target is
  replaced by the restored regular file and a link above the target
  aborts the restore, so rewind cannot write outside the workspace.
- Validate recorded paths and preflight the whole restore before any
  mutation; per-file writes go through a temp file and rename, which
  also replaces read-only targets atomically.
- Record the snapshot-time .gitignore setting, skipped paths, a
  full-prompt hash, and raw bytes for non-UTF-8 names in the manifest
  (version 3; legacy version 2 manifests still load).
- Delete exactly what the preview counted: the delete walk uses the
  snapshot-time setting against the current .gitignore contents, and
  the set is captured before the copy phase rewrites .gitignore.
- Skip unreadable files instead of failing the whole snapshot and
  surface failures and skips in the transcript.
- Resolve cross-conversation rewind fallbacks only when the prompt
  matches a single conversation; ambiguous matches decline to restore.
- Match prompts by full hash instead of the 200-char excerpt.
- Seed a conversation's first snapshot from the newest snapshot of any
  conversation in the workspace so resumed/forked conversations do not
  re-hash unchanged files.
- Prune interrupted snapshot directories and detect stale locks via the
  recorded process start time so recycled PIDs cannot block snapshots.
- Document the size+mtime fast-path tradeoff and keep snapshots
  synchronous before the turn so they always precede the turn's writes.
